            "We perform several analyses and ablation studies to identify the cause of this gap and find several avenues for agent improvement in the future including more robust search generation, explicit memory modules, and better handling of noisy web text. {\\color{black} Finally, we also demonstrate an instance of \\textit{sim-to-real} transfer by deploying agents trained with \\benchmark{} to operate on \\url{amazon.com} and \\url{ebay.com}, and find that they can achieve similar performances despite search engine and product differences, and consistently outperform the rule baseline of using the first result returned by the commercial search engines when directly searching the instruction texts.} This demonstrates the practical potential of our work towards developing agents that can operate autonomously on the world wide web (WWW).\n",
